# default document handlers, as a reproducible record.
#
# ⚠⚠ THIS FILE IS NOT APPLIED. writing it changes nothing; `duti` only reads it when invoked:
#
#     duti ~/.config/duti/defaults.duti          # apply every line
#     duti -x json                               # what actually handles .json right now
#
# it is deliberately left unapplied because file associations are a user preference, and six
# lines below (marked ✎) differ from this machine's state as measured on 2026-07-29. read those
# six, then apply — or edit them back to the current value first.
#
# format: <bundle-id>  <extension|UTI>  <role>.  duti reads an argument beginning with a dot as
# a filename extension; role is one of all / viewer / editor / shell / none.
#
# bundle ids used here:
#   com.colliderli.iina            IINA
#   com.apple.Preview              Preview
#   com.apple.Safari               Safari
#   com.aone.keka                  Keka
#   com.microsoft.VSCodeInsiders   VS Code Insiders
#   com.mitchellh.ghostty          Ghostty
#   org.godotengine.godot          Godot
#   org.blenderfoundation.blender  Blender
#   com.figma.DesktopBeta          Figma (beta channel)

# ── video and audio ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
com.colliderli.iina	.mp4	all
com.colliderli.iina	.mkv	all
com.colliderli.iina	.mov	all
com.colliderli.iina	.webm	all
com.colliderli.iina	.mp3	all
com.colliderli.iina	.flac	all
com.colliderli.iina	.wav	all

# ── images and documents ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
com.apple.Preview	.png	all
com.apple.Preview	.jpg	all
com.apple.Preview	.gif	all
com.apple.Preview	.webp	all
com.apple.Preview	.pdf	all
com.apple.Preview	.psd	all
# svg stays with safari: it renders correctly and scales, where preview rasterises.
com.apple.Safari	.svg	all

# ── archives ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
com.aone.keka	.zip	all
com.aone.keka	.7z	all
com.aone.keka	.rar	all

# ── creative tools ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
org.godotengine.godot	.godot	all
org.blenderfoundation.blender	.blend	all
com.figma.DesktopBeta	.fig	all

# ── code and config ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
com.microsoft.VSCodeInsiders	.md	all
com.microsoft.VSCodeInsiders	.yaml	all
com.microsoft.VSCodeInsiders	.yml	all
com.microsoft.VSCodeInsiders	.toml	all
com.microsoft.VSCodeInsiders	.py	all

# ✎ .json currently opens in Passepartout (com.algoritmico.ios.Passepartout), the wireguard
#   client — it claims the extension for its profile exports and won that race. almost
#   certainly not intended for every json on the machine.
com.microsoft.VSCodeInsiders	.json	all

# ✎ .ts currently opens in IINA, which claims it as an MPEG transport stream. correct for
#   broadcast captures, wrong for typescript, and typescript is what is on this machine.
com.microsoft.VSCodeInsiders	.ts	all

# ✎ .fish currently has no handler at all — double-clicking one does nothing.
com.microsoft.VSCodeInsiders	.fish	all

# ✎ .sh currently opens in Ghostty, which means double-clicking a shell script in Finder
#   RUNS it rather than showing it. editor is the safer default; run it from a shell instead.
com.microsoft.VSCodeInsiders	.sh	all

# ✎ .txt currently opens in TextEdit. harmless, but inconsistent with every other text format
#   here going to the editor that is actually configured.
com.microsoft.VSCodeInsiders	.txt	all

# ✎ .js and .css currently open in Safari, which views but cannot edit them. .html stays with
#   safari deliberately — opening a page to look at it is the common case.
com.microsoft.VSCodeInsiders	.js	all
com.microsoft.VSCodeInsiders	.css	all
com.apple.Safari	.html	all
